  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1014 AM CDT Wed Jul 15 2026\n\nThe greatest rain chances for the next several days will fall on\nFriday and Saturday. With a moist airmass and better forcing in\nplace, showers and storms will be more widespread. Low-level shear\nand mid-level lapse rates look unimpressive at this time, so the\nsevere threat is low. The main concern with any storm will be its\npotential to produce heavy rainfall, which could lead to localized\nflooding and ponding. \n\nTemperatures will continue trend up over the coming days with\nafternoon heat indices in the low 100s west of the Cumberland \nPlateau from Friday to Tuesday. Guidance is showing a cold front\ncrossing the area on Tuesday night, which would bring some relief\nfrom the hot temperatures over the weekend. A drier airmass moving\nin behind the front would also result in lower PoPs mid to late \nweek.",
